<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gisulf I of Friuli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">late 6th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gisulf I was the first <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/friuli">Friuli</a>, a nephew of King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a>, who left him at Forum Iulii, modern Cividale, around 568 to guard the passes into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> from the east. According to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paul-the-deacon">Paul the Deacon</a>, he asked for chosen Lombard families to settle with him, founding the duchy, which controlled the route from the Julian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alps">Alps</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gisulf-i-of-friuli.jpg" alt="Gisulf I of Friuli" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Steakley · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gisulf_cross.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
